\section*{Global Arthur enhancements of occurring excursion parameters}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that assuming the stated finite-level decomposition, each occurring cuspidal excursion parameter for a split semisimple function-field group has a global Arthur enhancement with one algebraic $\mathrm{SL}_2$ and a commuting Weil action, including inertia.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05), shtuka cohomology supplies a finite-type cyclic support carrying full excursion data. Frobenius-compatible coherent models of Iwahori categories at several places identify an open-orbit condition, which assembles a single commuting Weil and $\mathrm{SL}_2$ pair.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05).

\subsection{Formal verification}
